From 321da24b428ef8fe2a1a470f7b083020886241f1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 08:32:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(chat): a withheld claim stays with its own result
 card (UI-SEM-097 per-card carrier, NOT LOW)

Pre-review on #2004 (5829256617), confirmed on the mounted chain: a turn
whose typed leader_claim is withheld but whose block still names a leader
lost its refusal when a later Run permitted, because the card's only other
refusal source, the held report's producer_leader_permission, belongs to the
LATEST report. RC accepted this carrier as a follow-up after U4
(#69 5829442152 section 4).

`mapV5Blocks` now takes the turn's context and stamps
`leader_claim_permitted: false` on the v5_analysis_result block when the
turn's `analysis_state.leader_claim.permitted` is false, read by
`turnLeaderClaimPermitted` with the same AnalysisStateV1Schema that
applyV5State step 4 uses. It only ever withholds: a permitted or unknown
claim stamps nothing, so every other card is byte-identical. The one call
site (useConversation) passes the turn's analysis_state. The transcript
persists blocks, so the stamp survives a reload. The card withholds on the
stamp as well as the null id and the held report.

Tests (mounted chain, served 57f903c body, derived conflicting wire):
the mapper stamps false and nothing else; a withheld claim that kept its
id, then a permitted Run: the earlier card stays withheld; the same after
a reload from the saved transcript alone. Mutants: card ignores the stamp
(2 fail), call site passes no context (2 fail), mapper never stamps (3
fail). src/v5 + src/canvas/conversation: 376 files, 5192 tests green.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Q5bxkDMkNnEcRXKYsV9zEa
